# Live provider tests.
#
# Copy this file somewhere outside the repository, fill in the keys and the models, and point
# the suite at it:
#
#   LOOM_LIVE_ENV=~/live.env go test ./livetest/
#
# There is no default path: without LOOM_LIVE_ENV the suite skips, so `go test ./...` never
# reaches a provider and never spends a credential by accident.
#
# LOOM_LIVE_PROVIDERS names the provider blocks to run, in order: a block named "ark" is the
# modelfactory provider "ark" and is configured by the LOOM_LIVE_ARK_* variables. Drop a name
# from the list to skip that provider.
LOOM_LIVE_PROVIDERS=deepseek,zhipuai,ark,openrouter

# STRUCTURED_OUTPUT is optional and defaults to "json_object". Declare "json_schema" for a model
# whose endpoint enforces a schema: the suite then sends the schema in response_format and asserts
# the endpoint accepts it, so a capability a model does not have fails here instead of in
# production.
#
# MODELS is a comma-separated list, so one provider can cover several models: every model runs
# the same three flows. EFFORT is optional and defaults to "low"; leave it empty to enable
# reasoning without naming an effort. Every *_MODELS above stays empty in this file: it ships
# the shape of the configuration and leaves the choice to the operator, because what a credential
# may call, and what it may spend, is theirs. livetest/env_test.go fails if a model appears here
# or in the documentation.

LOOM_LIVE_DEEPSEEK_URL=https://api.deepseek.com/v1
LOOM_LIVE_DEEPSEEK_KEY=
LOOM_LIVE_DEEPSEEK_MODELS=

LOOM_LIVE_ZHIPUAI_URL=https://open.bigmodel.cn/api/paas/v4
LOOM_LIVE_ZHIPUAI_KEY=
LOOM_LIVE_ZHIPUAI_MODELS=

LOOM_LIVE_ARK_URL=https://ark.cn-beijing.volces.com/api/v3
LOOM_LIVE_ARK_KEY=
LOOM_LIVE_ARK_MODELS=

LOOM_LIVE_OPENROUTER_URL=https://openrouter.ai/api/v1
LOOM_LIVE_OPENROUTER_KEY=
LOOM_LIVE_OPENROUTER_MODELS=
